.TH WALLPAPER-CONTROLS 1 "October 2026" "Wallpaper-Controls @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wallpaper-controls \- preview and adjust GNOME wallpapers
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wallpaper-controls
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Wallpaper-Controls opens a graphical editor for wallpaper sizing, image
position, border color, light and dark images, and separate monitor images.
Changes are staged until the user presses Apply.
Requires GNOME with GTK 4.10 and libadwaita 1.4 or newer.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "\-\-set-wallpaper " IMAGE
Open the editor with a local image staged for both light and dark modes.
The user must press Apply to change the desktop.
.TP
.B \-\-show-background-color
Open the editor with a visible border staged.
.TP
.B \-\-watch-displays
Run the optional monitor helper, used by the app's login entry.
.TP
.B \-\-quit
Ask the running application to quit. Pending edits require confirmation.
.TP
.BR \-\-version ", " \-V
Print the application version.
.TP
.BR \-\-help ", " \-h
Print usage information.
.SH FILES
Preferences are stored in
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/wallpaper-controls/monitors.json ,
or in ~/.config/wallpaper-controls/monitors.json when XDG_CONFIG_HOME is unset.
Generated wallpapers are stored in
.IR $XDG_DATA_HOME/wallpaper-controls/generated/ ,
or in ~/.local/share/wallpaper-controls/generated/ when XDG_DATA_HOME is unset.
Removing the package preserves these personal files.
